9946030?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma","html_url":"https://github.com/lyuma","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-18T11:20:24Z","updated_at":"2025-12-18T11:21:25Z","body":"I'm having a difficult time understand the exact usecase or problem this is solving.\r\n\r\nI understand the principle of being able to generate a skin from a rest pose (similar to how blender's edit mode works when defining an Armature). But I'm having a difficult time understanding when a user would need to do this within the import flow.\r\n\r\nUsually when we add a new feature or functionality, it should link to an issue it's solving or a proposal it is implementing which answers these questions.\r\n\r\nWould it be possible to link to (*one or more of*) a reference (paper, example of another engine with this feature or bug report), a video or screenshots, or include an example project showing how this can be used? Basically, I want to understand who the target audience is for this feature, so I can evaluate if the user interface makes sense for that audience or if there is a way to simplify the feature to solve the problem you are running into.\r\n\r\nFor now if you want to edit this PR description to contain this information that could be fine to start with. I'm not asking you for all of the above, just something","aut